│ at least five newly diagnosed patients per year. All consecutive adult (⩾ 18 yr) patients seen between October 2002  │
│ and October 2003 were to be included.Main Results: A total of 674 patients (mean ± SD age, 50 ± 15 yr; range, 18–85  │
│ yr) were entered in the registry. Idiopathic, familial, anorexigen, connective tissue diseases, congenital heart     │
│ diseases, portal hypertension, and HIV-associated PAH accounted for 39.2, 3.9, 9.5, 15.3, 11.3, 10.4, and 6.2% of    │
